<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                   xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_MountDependency"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="author" name="Author"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="build-pipeline" name="Build pipeline"/>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Remote-mount a harness and its dependency closure.

       No git submodules, ever; no `.deps/`. A remote
       mount is a DECLARED DIRECTORY with a remote source pinned to a
       40-character SHA. The defaults (which directories, where) live in the
       harness's own declaration; a downstream may override them by id,
       never by path; the closure is resolved transitively; code arrives
       through the mounted code directories.

       Executed by `bun run cat mount:remote` (and by `state:mount`, which the
       session-start hook runs). Checked offline by `mount:remote:check`.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:process id="Process_MountDependency" name="Remote-mount a dependency" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Laying a harness — and every instance it needs — down from another repository at a pinned commit, as declared directories, with a lock that says exactly what arrived.

You are in this process whenever a folio or harness needs a layer it does not hold: a downstream folio built on a content layer above this harness, a separated instance whose foundation lives elsewhere. The downstream names the harness, its repository and a 40-character pin as a `source.remote` instance in its root `index.config.json` (legacy: `remoteMounts` on its declaration, never both); everything else is read from the harness's own declaration at that pin.

Every instance reached ends in one of three states — mounted, missing, could-not-determine — and the third is never reported as the first. The skill is `remote-mount`.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_MountDependency">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Author" name="Downstream author" partitionElementRef="author">
        <bpmn:documentation>A person decides WHICH harness and WHICH pin, and whether to override a default. Nothing below chooses a pin: a branch name is refused, and so is an abbreviated SHA.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_LayerNeeded</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_DeclareMount</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Pipeline" name="Build pipeline" partitionElementRef="build-pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Mechanical from the declaration on: the same declaration mounts the same bytes in every container, and only an override by id changes where or what.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ResolveClosure</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_MountInstances</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_WriteLock</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RenderAgentSurface</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CheckAgainstLock</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_State</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Mounted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Reported</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_LayerNeeded" name="A layer this&#10;checkout does not hold"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_DeclareMount" name="Declare the mount:&#10;harness, repository, pin">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        An instance `{ name, source: { remote: { repository, ref } } }` in the
        downstream's root `index.config.json`, written through
        `writeDeclaredMounts`. A folio with no index still reads `remoteMounts`
        on its declaration; both at once is refused. `ref` is a full
        40-character commit. Overrides, if any, are keyed by instance name and
        then by directory id — never by path. The index itself is the
        index-config skill's.
        Decide first whether you want a remote mount at all: reading another
        graph without holding its code is a SUBSCRIPTION, not a mount.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="remote-mount"/><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="index-config"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_ResolveClosure" name="Resolve the closure&#10;at the pin">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Fetch the pinned tree (shallow, blobless). Read the harness's declaration
        from it; for each `needs` name, find that instance in the same tree, else
        follow a GITLINK at that tree as a pin into its own repository. A need
        found in neither is missing; one the downstream already holds is local.
        Paths and directories come from `mountDefaults` unless overridden.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="remote-mount"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_MountInstances" name="Mount each instance&#10;at its declared path">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Sparse checkout of the declaration and the chosen directories, copied to
        the mount path (by default the instance's home path, so relative imports
        and sibling discovery hold). Never onto tracked bytes; never onto a
        directory no lock says this mount made; never over edits to a previous
        mount — those are left untouched and reported. A replay of the lock
        tries the index's layers cache ref first (`refs/cat/layers/&lt;key&gt;`,
        then `refs/cat/layers/main`): one shallow fetch, every byte verified
        against the lock, and any layer that does not verify is fetched from its
        own repository.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="remote-mount"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_WriteLock" name="Write the lock">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        `index.lock.json` beside the downstream's `index.config.json` (the
        legacy `&lt;instance&gt;.mount-lock.json` is still read, and is renamed
        onto the new name when rewritten; both present is an error): the
        pins it was written for, each instance's repository, SHA and how the pin
        was found, each directory's tree digest — and what was NOT mounted, with
        why, so an offline check cannot read a gap as clean. Whoever writes the
        lock writes its layers cache ref (`layers:publish`, which refuses unless
        every mount hashes to the lock); on main, the index's workflow does it.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="remote-mount"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RenderAgentSurface" name="Re-render the&#10;agent surface">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        When the lock changed, the layers an agent's skills and memory are
        generated from changed with it. `mount:remote` re-runs the generators
        of what an agent actually reads — `skill:commands` (`.claude/commands/`)
        and `agent-memory` (`.claude/agent-memory/` and the `.agents/` copies)
        — from the checkout root, and a generator that fails fails the run.
        A re-pin commit therefore carries the new layers AND the surface
        rendered from them, because new layers shipped without their
        rendered surface fail the agent-memory tests.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="remote-mount"/><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="agent-memory"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_CheckAgainstLock" name="Check disk against&#10;lock against declaration">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        `mount:remote:check`, with no network: the lock's pins are the
        declaration's, and every locked directory is on disk and hashes to its
        digest. Could-not-determine outranks missing, which outranks mounted.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="remote-mount"/><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="ci-health"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_State" name="Every instance&#10;mounted or local?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Read off the check's aggregate state. `skipped` and `local` are answers; `missing` and `could-not-determine` are not.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Mounted" name="The closure is on disk,&#10;pinned and locked"/>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Reported" name="Reported loudly:&#10;missing / could not determine"/>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D1" sourceRef="Start_LayerNeeded" targetRef="Task_DeclareMount"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D2" sourceRef="Task_DeclareMount" targetRef="Task_ResolveClosure"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D3" sourceRef="Task_ResolveClosure" targetRef="Task_MountInstances"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D4" sourceRef="Task_MountInstances" targetRef="Task_WriteLock"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D5" sourceRef="Task_WriteLock" targetRef="Task_RenderAgentSurface"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D5b" sourceRef="Task_RenderAgentSurface" targetRef="Task_CheckAgainstLock"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D6" sourceRef="Task_CheckAgainstLock" targetRef="GW_State"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D7" name="yes" sourceRef="GW_State" targetRef="End_Mounted"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_D8" name="no" sourceRef="GW_State" targetRef="End_Reported"/>

  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_MountDependency">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_MountDependency" bpmnElement="Process_MountDependency">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Lane_Author" bpmnElement="Lane_Author" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="40" width="1240" height="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Lane_Pipeline" bpmnElement="Lane_Pipeline" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="260" width="1240" height="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Start_LayerNeeded" bpmnElement="Start_LayerNeeded">
        <dc:Bounds x="216" y="122" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="196" y="163" width="80" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_DeclareMount" bpmnElement="Task_DeclareMount">
        <dc:Bounds x="292" y="80" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_ResolveClosure" bpmnElement="Task_ResolveClosure">
        <dc:Bounds x="292" y="290" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_MountInstances" bpmnElement="Task_MountInstances">
        <dc:Bounds x="452" y="290" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_WriteLock" bpmnElement="Task_WriteLock">
        <dc:Bounds x="612" y="290" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_RenderAgentSurface" bpmnElement="Task_RenderAgentSurface">
        <dc:Bounds x="772" y="290" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_Task_CheckAgainstLock" bpmnElement="Task_CheckAgainstLock">
        <dc:Bounds x="932" y="290" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_GW_State" bpmnElement="GW_State" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1092" y="325" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1060" y="264" width="114" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_End_Mounted" bpmnElement="End_Mounted">
        <dc:Bounds x="1197" y="332" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="323" width="150" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="S_End_Reported" bpmnElement="End_Reported">
        <dc:Bounds x="1197" y="422" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="413" width="150" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D1" bpmnElement="F_D1">
        <di:waypoint x="252" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="292" y="140" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D2" bpmnElement="F_D2">
        <di:waypoint x="352" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="352" y="290" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D3" bpmnElement="F_D3">
        <di:waypoint x="412" y="350" />
        <di:waypoint x="452" y="350" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D4" bpmnElement="F_D4">
        <di:waypoint x="572" y="350" />
        <di:waypoint x="612" y="350" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D5" bpmnElement="F_D5">
        <di:waypoint x="732" y="350" />
        <di:waypoint x="772" y="350" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D5b" bpmnElement="F_D5b">
        <di:waypoint x="892" y="350" />
        <di:waypoint x="932" y="350" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D6" bpmnElement="F_D6">
        <di:waypoint x="1052" y="350" />
        <di:waypoint x="1092" y="350" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D7" bpmnElement="F_D7">
        <di:waypoint x="1142" y="350" />
        <di:waypoint x="1197" y="350" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1152" y="330" width="30" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="E_F_D8" bpmnElement="F_D8">
        <di:waypoint x="1117" y="375" />
        <di:waypoint x="1117" y="440" />
        <di:waypoint x="1197" y="440" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1122" y="395" width="25" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
